# Modular Monolith Architecture (ADR-002)

All domains live in one deployable unit under `app/domains/`. Shared infrastructure only in `app/core/`.

## Domain Modules

| Domain | Path | Responsibility |
|--------|------|----------------|
| ingestion | `app/domains/ingestion/` | ARQ poller, adapters, normalizer, repository |
| engine | `app/domains/engine/` | Rule pack, calculators, state machine, sweeper, replay |
| notifier | `app/domains/notifier/` | Redis subscriber, Twilio Voice/SMS, alert suppression |
| dashboard | `app/domains/dashboard/` | REST API, HTMX UI, day grid / alert helpers |
| billing | `app/domains/billing/` | SaaS tier schemas; gates live in `app/core/billing.py` |

## Domain File Layout

Each domain follows this structure when applicable:

- `schemas.py` — Pydantic v2 DTOs (API + internal contracts)
- `models.py` — SQLAlchemy ORM models
- `repository.py` — Data access (class with `AsyncSession`)
- `router.py` / `ui.py` — FastAPI routes (dashboard)
- `adapters/` — Provider-specific code (ingestion only)

## Import Boundaries

- ✅ Cross-domain imports allowed (e.g. engine imports ingestion schemas/models)
- ✅ All domains import from `app/core/` for config, database, redis, security, billing gates
- ❌ Never put business logic in `app/core/` (billing *gates* are OK; tier catalogs stay in `domains/billing`)
- ❌ Never import provider-specific adapter code into `engine/` or `notifier/`
- ❌ Do not add new code to legacy root scripts (`geotab_ingestor.py`); use `dcw-backend/`
